---
title: "Activities & the surrounding area"
description: "Things to do at the Château de la Huberdière and in the surrounding area: heated swimming pool, Italian cookery classes, hot-air balloon rides, the châteaux of the Loire Valley, the Vouvray vineyards and walks in Touraine, just ten minutes from Amboise."
---

Both at the château and in the surrounding area, the days slip by effortlessly. The fourteen-hectare estate is just as much about the outdoors as it is about the indoors, and from Touraine, the most beautiful châteaux of the Loire, the vineyards and the riverbanks are all within easy driving distance. Here’s everything you need to plan your stay, just ten minutes from Amboise and 2 hours 20 minutes from Paris.

## At the château itself

You can spend a whole day at the château without ever getting bored, or having to get back in the car. The walled grounds are perfect for a stroll: a 16 × 3-metre swimming lane heated from April to October, its pool house, paths through the woods and vineyards, a permaculture vegetable patch and flower gardens where you can pick herbs for your evening meal.

- Heated swimming pool from April to October and pool house
- A walk through the estate’s woods and vineyards
- Permaculture vegetable garden and flower gardens
- Pétanque, table tennis and golf nearby
- Eclectic library and board games

Inside, music takes centre stage: a concert grand piano, an electric piano, guitars, a bass and a drum kit await those who play, or those who wish to take it up again. Two experiences can be booked in advance and often form a highlight of guests’ stays: an Italian cookery class with Lodovica, exploring her heritage and market produce, and a relaxing massage without having to leave the estate. Every day, our team is on hand to help with any details regarding your holiday or event. Ask for our road book, packed with places to visit, experiences and top tips. Pets welcome on request.

## Around the castle

Touraine has something for everyone, from cultural heritage to the great outdoors, and can be explored at the pace of the Loire. We work with trusted local partners, whom we book on your behalf.

- Bike hire with Loire Bikes, on the Loire à Vélo cycle route
- Wine tastings at the Tasting Room and at Mondomaine
- Hot-air balloon flight departing from the castle with Art Montgolfière
- Canoeing on the Cher with Canoë Aventure
- Traditional sailing boat on the Loire with Millière Raboton

The vineyards of Vouvray and Montlouis-sur-Loire are just a few minutes away: cave cellars, the autumn grape harvest, and wine tastings at the winemakers’ estates. The market in Amboise, the cave-dwelling villages and the banks of the Loire round off days that don’t need to be packed full to be fulfilling.

## The châteaux of the Loire within easy reach

Amboise and the Clos Lucé, Leonardo da Vinci’s final resting place, are ten minutes away. On the other side of the river, La Huberdière is an ideal base from which to explore the surrounding area without ever having to drive for long. Chenonceau, the château perched over the River Cher, can be reached in twenty minutes. Chaumont-sur-Loire and its garden festival, Cheverny, Blois, Villandry and its gardens, and Chambord can all be visited in a single day.

To plan a tour, we’ll help you choose based on the season and the time you have available. Our guide to [visiting the châteaux of the Loire Valley](/en/blog/visiter-chateaux-de-la-loire) suggests an initial itinerary, and the château’s road book provides the rest.

## Frequently Asked Questions

**Is the swimming pool heated and open all year round?**
The 16 × 3 m swimming lane is heated from April to October. Outside this period, the pool house and grounds remain open, but the swimming pool is not in use.

**Do I need to book activities in advance?**
The Italian cookery class, massages and activities offered by our partners (hot-air balloon rides, cycling, canoeing, tastings) must be booked in advance. We’ll take care of this for you; just let us know what you’d like to do before you arrive.

**Which castles can you visit in a day from La Huberdière?**
Amboise and the Clos Lucé are ten minutes away, Chenonceau twenty. Chaumont-sur-Loire, Cheverny, Blois, Villandry and Chambord can all be visited in a day, either individually or as part of a tour.

**Are there any activities for children?**
Yes: a swimming pool, bikes, canoeing, pétanque and table tennis in the park, not to mention family-friendly castle tours, such as the Clos Lucé and its Leonardo da Vinci machines.

**Are pets allowed?**
Pets are welcome on request. Please let us know when you book so that we can make the best possible arrangements for your stay.
